"],["מִתְחַבֵּא","mitchabe'","H2244","HVtrmsa","hiding"],["שֵׁשׁ","shesh","H8337","HNcbsc","six"],["שָׁנִים","shanim","H8141","HNcmpa","years"],["וַעֲתַלְיָה","va'atalyah","H6271","HC/Npf","and Athaliah"],["מֹלֶכֶת","molekhet","H4427","HVqrfsa","[was] reigning"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","over"],["הָאָרֶץ","ha'aretz","H776","HTd/Ncfsa","the land"]],"x":[[24012001,24012001,3]],"xn":1}},"people":[{"id":"ahaziah_121","name":"Ahaziah","also":"Jehoahaz, Azariah","summary":"The son of Joram, or Jehoram, and sixth king of Judah. Called Jehoahaz (2 Chr. 21:17; 25:23), and Azariah (2 Chr. 22:6). Guided by his idolatrous mother Athaliah, his reign was disastrous (2 Kings 8:24-29; 9:29).","verses":26,"father":"Jehoram","mother":"Athaliah","v":[1,2,6,7,8,9,10,11]},{"id":"jehoram_803","name":"Jehoram","also":"Joram","summary":"The eldest son and successor of Jehoshaphat, king of Judah. He reigned eight years (B.C. 892-885) alone as king of Judah, having been previously for some years associated with his father (2 Chr. 21:5, 20; 2 Kings 8:16).","verses":16,"father":"Jehoshaphat","mother":"","v":[1,11]},{"id":"athaliah_359","name":"Athaliah","also":"","summary":"The daughter of Ahab and Jezebel, and the wife of Jehoram, king of Judah (2 Kings 8:18), who “walked in the ways of the house of Ahab” (2 Chr. 21:6), called “daughter” of Omri (2 Kings 8:26).","verses":15,"father":"Ahab","mother":"Jezebel","v":[2,10,11,12]},{"id":"omri_2243","name":"Omri","also":"","summary":"Servant of Jehovah. When Elah was murdered by Zimri at Tirzah (1 Kings 16:15-27), Omri, his captain, was made king (B.C. 931). For four years there was continued opposition to his reign, Tibni, another claimant to the throne, leading the opposing party; but at the close of that period all his rivals were defeated, and he became king of Israel, “Tibni died and Omri reigned” (B.C. 927).","verses":13,"father":"","mother":"","v":[2]},{"id":"ahab_113","name":"Ahab","also":"","summary":"The son of Omri, whom he succeeded as the seventh king of Israel. His history is recorded in 1 Kings 16-22. His wife was Jezebel, who exercised a very evil influence over him.","verses":80,"father":"Omri","mother":"","v":[3,4,5,6,7,8]},{"id":"hazael_1463","name":"Hazael","also":"","summary":"Whom God beholds, an officer of Ben-hadad II., king of Syria, who ultimately came to the throne, according to the word of the Lord to Elijah (1 Kings 19:15), after he had put the king to death (2 Kings 8:15).","verses":21,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5,6]},{"id":"joram_804","name":"Joram","also":"Jehoram","summary":"The son of Ahab and Jezebel, and successor to his brother Ahaziah on the throne of Israel. He reigned twelve years, B.C. 896-884 (2 Kings 1:17; 3:1).","verses":19,"father":"Ahab","mother":"Jezebel","v":[5,6,7]},{"id":"jehu_817","name":"Jehu","also":"","summary":"King of Israel, the son of Jehoshaphat (2 Kings 9:2), and grandson of Nimshi. The story of his exaltation to the throne is deeply interesting.","verses":47,"father":"Jehoshaphat","mother":"","v":[7,8,9]},{"id":"nimshi_2207","name":"Nimshi","also":"","summary":"Saved.","verses":5,"father":"","mother":"","v":[7]},{"id":"jehoshaphat_808","name":"Jehoshaphat","also":"Josaphat","summary":"The son and successor of Asa, king of Judah. After fortifying his kingdom against Israel (2 Chr. 17:1, 2), he set himself to cleanse the land of idolatry (1 Kings 22:43).","verses":69,"father":"Asa","mother":"Azubah","v":[9]},{"id":"jehoiada_793","name":"Jehoiada","also":"Barachias","summary":"The high priest at the time of Athaliah’s usurpation of the throne of Judah.","verses":26,"father":"","mother":"","v":[11]},{"id":"joash_1632","name":"Joash","also":"Jehoash","summary":"The son of King Ahaziah. While yet an infant, he was saved from the general massacre of the family by his aunt Jehosheba, and was apparently the only surviving descendant of Solomon (2 Chr. 21:4, 17).","verses":19,"father":"Ahaziah","mother":"Zibiah","v":[11]},{"id":"jehoshabeath_811","name":"Jehoshabeath","also":"Jehosheba","summary":"Jehovah-swearing, the daughter of Jehoram, the king of Israel. She is called Jehoshabeath in 2 Chr. 22:11.","verses":2,"father":"Jehoram","mother":"Athaliah","v":[11]}],"places":[{"id":"jerusalem_636","name":"Jerusalem","kind":"City","lat":31.77667,"lon":35.23417,"summary":"Called also Salem, Ariel, Jebus, the “city of God,” the “holy city;” by the modern Arabs el-Khuds, meaning “the holy;” once “the city of Judah” (2 Chr. 25:28).","verses":754,"v":[1,2]},{"id":"ramoth-gilead_984","name":"Ramoth-gilead","kind":"City","lat":32.56527,"lon":36.00556,"summary":"Heights of Gilead, a city of refuge on the east of Jordan; called “Ramoth in Gilead” (Deut. 4:43; Josh. 20:8; 21:38). Here Ahab, who joined Jehoshaphat in an endeavour to rescue it from the hands of the king of Syria, was mortally wounded (1 Kings 22:1-36).","verses":20,"v":[5]},{"id":"syria_1122","name":"Syria","kind":"Region (Country)","lat":37.5,"lon":37.5,"summary":"(Heb. Aram), the name in the Old Testament given to the whole country which lay to the north-east of Phoenicia, extending to beyond the Euphrates and the Tigris.","verses":64,"v":[5,6]},{"id":"jezreel_643","name":"Jezreel","kind":"Amphitheatre,theatre,settlement","lat":32.50207,"lon":35.50196,"summary":"A town of Issachar (Josh. 19:18), where the kings of Israel often resided (1 Kings 18:45; 21:1; 2 Kings 9:30). Here Elijah met Ahab, Jehu, and Bidkar; and here Jehu executed his dreadful commission against the house of Ahab (2 Kings 9:14-37; 10:1-11).","verses":22,"v":[6]},{"id":"ramah_976","name":"Ramah","kind":"","lat":32.56527,"lon":36.00556,"summary":"The same as Ramoth-gilead, 2 Kings 8:29; 2 Chr. 22:6.","verses":2,"v":[6]},{"id":"samaria_1022","name":"Samaria","kind":"Region","lat":32.33142,"lon":35.22859,"summary":"A watch-mountain or a watch-tower. In the heart of the mountains of Israel, a few miles north-west of Shechem, stands the “hill of Shomeron,” a solitary mountain, a great “mamelon.”","ve